## 8. Order Service Configuration

Order Service has two responsibilities:

- Produce `OrderCreatedEvent`.
- Consume `InventoryUpdatedEvent`.

For the current local setup:

```yaml
spring:
  kafka:
    bootstrap-servers: localhost:9092

    producer:
      key-serializer: org.apache.kafka.common.serialization.StringSerializer
      value-serializer: io.confluent.kafka.serializers.KafkaAvroSerializer
      properties:
        schema.registry.url: http://localhost:8081

    consumer:
      group-id: order-group
      key-deserializer: org.apache.kafka.common.serialization.StringDeserializer
      value-deserializer: io.confluent.kafka.serializers.KafkaAvroDeserializer
      properties:
        schema.registry.url: http://localhost:8081
        specific.avro.reader: true
```

### Producer

```java
kafkaTemplate.send("order-created-topic", orderCreatedEvent);
```

### Consumer

```java
@KafkaListener(
    topics = "inventory-updated-topic",
    groupId = "order-group"
)
public void listen(InventoryUpdatedEvent event) {

    System.out.println("Order ID: " + event.getOrderId());
    System.out.println("Inventory Status: " + event.getStatus());

    // Update order status in database.
}
```

